# Cloudflare Pages headers
#
# CRITICAL: Never set Cache-Control: immutable (or long max-age) on /app/* path
# rules. If Cloudflare's SPA soft-404 returns index.html for a missing hashed
# asset URL, that HTML would be cached forever under the .js path → white screen
# ("Unexpected token '<'"). Hashed files already cache well via CF defaults.
#
# Also never force Content-Type on /app/*.js — same poison path would label HTML
# as JavaScript and the browser would try to execute it.

# Google Identity Services popup needs postMessage back to opener.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups

# SPA shell must always revalidate so clients pick up new /app/*.js hashes.
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate

/logo.png
  Content-Type: image/png
